      <accessrestrict id="aspace_9ab59a4abfe6e653884581063eab4da6">
         <head>Conditions Governing Access</head>
         <p>Open for research.</p>
      </accessrestrict>
      <acqinfo id="aspace_157d45165ecb1ab2de13f0242369445e">
         <head>Immediate Source of Acquisition</head>
         <p>Gift of the Vietnamese Students Association.</p>
      </acqinfo>
      <arrangement id="aspace_65e818c300bcde652519db6198bdb6a4">
         <head>Arrangement</head>
         <p>The records are arranged alphebtically by subject, with photographs at the end.</p>
      </arrangement>
      <bioghist id="aspace_ce979c16c7504b4abdba9953373b0d3c">
         <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
         <p>The Vietnamese Students Association was founded in 1988 and hosts a wide range of events highlighting various aspects of Vietnamese culture and lived experience, including an annual cultural showcase. In the 1990s, the organization advocated for the creation of a Vietnamese language program.</p>
      </bioghist>
      <odd id="aspace_d2ca4b1859508164eea34bbbd677e774">
         <head>General</head>
         <p>Forms part of Yale Record Group 40 (YRG 40), Records of Yale clubs, societies and organizations.</p>
      </odd>
      <prefercite id="aspace_8af8b5ded1daad5e4f62709cb86ebd0a">
         <head>Preferred Citation</head>
         <p>Vietnamese Students Association at Yale (ViSA) records (RU 1218). Manuscripts and Archives, Yale University Library.</p>
      </prefercite>
      <scopecontent id="aspace_26d104d2c9996911741c0741197ed641">
         <head>Scope and Contents</head>
         <p>Materials primarily consists of fliers, photographsm and scrapbooks documenting events hosted by ViSA. Additional ogranizational records  include those documenting advocacy for the Vietnamese language program, meeting materials, and membership lists.</p>
      </scopecontent>
      <userestrict id="aspace_81d604a4e9a791a48eb46e6e1c5b062b">
         <head>Conditions Governing Use</head>
         <p>Copyright is retained by the Vietnamese Student Association for unpublished works they have authored or otherwise produced. If the organization ceases to exist, copyright passes to Yale University. Copyright status for other collection materials is unknown. Transmission or reproduction of materials protected by U.S. Copyright Law (Title 17, U.S.C.) beyond that allowed by fair use requires the written permission of the copyright owners. Works not in the public domain cannot be commercially exploited without permission of the copyright owners. Responsibility for any use rests exclusively with the user.</p>
      </userestrict>
